/ActualText (A box-plot of situational sleepiness over seven time points showing significantly increasing sleepiness from evening arrival to Morning and from start driving to 30 and 60 minutes into driving. On top of the box-plot a bar chart indicates the increasing percentage of participants suffering from microsleep from timepoint to timepoint.)
/A 45 0 R
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/S /Figure
/T ()
/Pg 32 0 R
/Alt (A box-plot of situational sleepiness over seven time points showing significantly increasing sleepiness from evening arrival to Morning and from start driving to 30 and 60 minutes into driving. On top of the box-plot a bar chart indicates the increasing percentage of participants suffering from microsleep from timepoint to timepoint.)
>>
endobj
17 0 obj
<<
/ActualText (On top, a composition of ten facial expressions from different participants of microsleep events during driving. On the bottom left, a pie-chart indicating a 74% proportion of participants were microsleep vulnerable and on the right a box-plot visualizes the distribution of time to microsleep of those vulnerable.)
/A 46 0 R
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/S /Figure
/T ()
/Pg 33 0 R
/Alt (On top, a composition of ten facial expressions from different participants of microsleep events during driving. On the bottom left, a pie-chart indicating a 74% proportion of participants were microsleep vulnerable and on the right a box-plot visualizes the distribution of time to microsleep of those vulnerable.)
>>
endobj
18 0 obj
<<
/ActualText (A box-plot indicating the increasing sleepiness of participants over time grouped by microsleep resistant and microsleep vulnerable participants. Vulnerable drivers show a steeper increase in sleepiness after start driving compared to microsleep resistant drivers.)
/A 47 0 R
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/S /Figure
/T ()
/Pg 34 0 R
/Alt (A box-plot indicating the increasing sleepiness of participants over time grouped by microsleep resistant and microsleep vulnerable participants. Vulnerable drivers show a steeper increase in sleepiness after start driving compared to microsleep resistant drivers.)
>>
